    {
      "@id": "#claim",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "name": "Entry 45: what should ε₀ be? — a contest of ride-level summaries",
      "text": "Out of sample on 513 held-out rides, the grade-inverse δ = k/s̄ with k = 0.0051 beats the frozen constant, winning 344/513 (p < 1e-4) and cutting held-out deficit error 0.067 → 0.055. Its domain is real descents only: k/s̄ exceeds 1 below s̄ ≈ 0.51%, so the form is defined for s̄ ≥ 3%. A companion flat-terrain probe was retracted mid-entry — it had selected segments on RAW ascent whose target rate sat below the corpus noise floor, making the search self-reinforcing; rebuilt on deadband-smoothed cells.",
      "appearance": [
        {
          "@id": "https://github.com/danlessa/bicycling-energy-model/blob/main/research/journal/MODEL_COMPARISON_JOURNAL.md"
        }
      ],
      "subjectOf": {
        "@id": "https://github.com/danlessa/bicycling-energy-model/blob/main/research/notes/claims.ttl"
      }
    },
